<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" article-type="research-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">Diagn Ther Endosc</journal-id><journal-title>Diagnostic and Therapeutic Endoscopy</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">1070-3608</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1029-0516</issn><publisher><publisher-name>Hindawi Publishing Corporation</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">18493370</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2362491</article-id>		<article-id pub-id-type="pii">S107036089500018X</article-id>		<article-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1155/DTE.1.227</article-id>	<article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Research Article</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>Severe Bronchomalacia in a 65-Year-Old Man Treated WithStent Insertion Instead of Surgical Bronchoplasty</article-title></title-group><contrib-group>		<contrib contrib-type="author" corresp="yes"><name><surname>Sutedja</surname><given-names>Tom G.</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff1">1</xref><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff2">2</xref></contrib>		<contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>de Graaf</surname><given-names>Jan C.</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff1">1</xref></contrib>		<contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Schramel</surname><given-names>Franz M.</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff1">1</xref></contrib>		<contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Van Kralingen</surname><given-names>Klaas W.</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff1">1</xref></contrib>		<contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Postmus</surname><given-names>Pieter E.</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff1">1</xref></contrib>	</contrib-group>		<aff id="aff1"><label>1</label>			<addr-line>Departments of Pulmonary Medicine ziekenhuis de Heel</addr-line>			<addr-line> Zaandam and the Free University Hospital Amsterdam</addr-line>			<country>The Netherlands</country>		</aff>		<aff id="aff2"><label>2</label>			<addr-line>FCCP</addr-line>			<addr-line>Department of Pulmonary Medicine</addr-line>			<addr-line>Free University Hospital</addr-line>			<addr-line> P.O. Box 7057</addr-line>			<addr-line>Amsterdam</addr-line>			<addr-line>1000 MB</addr-line>			<country>The Netherlands</country>		</aff>	<pub-date pub-type="ppub"><year>1995</year></pub-date><volume>1</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>227</fpage><lpage>228</lpage><history><date date-type="received"><day>22</day><month>4</month><year>1994</year></date><date date-type="accepted"><day>24</day><month>10</month><year>1994</year></date></history><permissions><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9; 1995 Hindawi Publishing Corporation.</copyright-statement><copyright-year>1995</copyright-year><copyright-holder>Hindawi Publishing Corporation</copyright-holder><license license-type="open-access" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/"><p>This is an open access article distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution License, which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.</p></license></permissions><abstract>		<p>Bronchomalacia in adults is rare. A case is reported here of a 65-year-old man with severe cough and mucostasis, caused by a benign bronchomalacia of the ventral wall of the left main bronchus. Thiswas treated successfully with the insertion of a silicone Dumon stent as an alternative to surgicalbronchoplasty.</p>	</abstract></article-meta></front></article>